==Notes==
*The Bit golems boost the power of N.O.X.'s spells, but the spells can be interrupted.  A good team of interrupters can shut down most of N.O.X.'s damage capability. Using this method makes destroying the golems useless, so you can focus all of your damage on him. However, when N.O.X. transits to the third stage, all the remaining golems will self-destruct and possibly deal heavy damage to your party. You may also want to get rid of any [[Rectifier Bit Golem]]s, as they will heal N.O.X. over time.
*Consider using skills that inflict [[daze]] such as [[Broad Head Arrow]] or [[Stunning Strike]] to increase your chances of interrupting N.O.X.'s spells.  A [[hero]] with [[Psychic Distraction]] is very effective as well.
*Armor-ignoring damage, health degeneration and [[Pain Inverter]] are effective against him.
*Like most golems, N.O.X. has no [[flesh]], and thus it is immune to [[bleeding]], [[disease]] and [[poison]].
*N.O.X has 56.760 health

==Trivia==
*The N.O.X. Divider Drive skill is likely a reference to one of the moves of GaoGaiGar, the titular mecha of the 90's super robot anime Yuusha-Oh GaoGaiGar.
*Nox, the Latin word for "night," is likely a reference to ''[[Guild Wars Nightfall]]''.

